Treat call targets 2-4 GB above JIT code as far

IsWithin2G accepted any distance that fits in 32 unsigned bits. A target
2-4 GB above the code was then called with a rel32, which Xbyak refuses
with "offset is too big", and a target just below the code always went
through rax. Check the signed range, as xbyak_util.h and dynarmic's
emit_x64.cpp do.

--- a/src/common/x64/xbyak.h
+++ b/src/common/x64/xbyak.h
@@ -264,7 +264,7 @@
 
 constexpr bool IsWithin2G(uintptr_t ref, uintptr_t target) noexcept {
     u64 const distance = target - (ref + 5);
-    return (distance & 0xffff'ffff) == distance;
+    return !(distance >= 0x8000'0000ULL && distance <= ~0x8000'0000ULL);
 }
 
 template <typename T>
